{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdd system-wide CPU usage and memory usage history graphs to the Procs page, plus small per-process CPU% / RSS sparklines for the selected process in the detail pane. Read-only.\n\n## Spec\n\n- **Data**: extend the existing snapshot (`sysinfo`, taken every `procs-refresh-interval`) with system CPU% (`global_cpu_usage`, optionally per core) and `used_memory` / `total_memory` (+ swap), accumulated in a ring buffer (default 120 samples = 4 minutes at 2 s). No accumulation while the page is not active (ticks are per active page).\n- **`graphs` pane** (new; added to the `page \"procs\"` layout, default height 6–8 rows above the process list or below the detail):\n  - CPU: time series drawn with `ratatui::widgets::Sparkline` (or a braille `Chart`), labelled with the current value and the recent peak. `c` toggles a per-core view (one small bar per core).\n  - Memory: used / total over the same width, labelled `3.2G / 16.0G (20%)`; one extra line for swap when present.\n  - Right-aligned while the buffer is not full yet.\n- **Detail pane**: one-line sparklines of the selected process's CPU% and RSS (keyed by pid; dropped when the process disappears).\n- **Config**: top-level `procs-history` (sample count, default 120), validated like `procs-refresh-interval`.\n- `VIG_PROCS_ROOT_PID` (recording filter) does not affect the system-wide graphs — they are machine totals; they carry no hostnames or paths, so recordings stay clean.\n- Secrets: numbers only, no new strings are displayed.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Snapshot gains system CPU / memory (+ per core); ring buffer as a pure struct with tests\n- [ ] `graphs` pane (KDL layout / tabs, `c` toggle)\n- [ ] Per-process sparklines in the detail pane\n- [ ] `procs-history` config + validation + tests\n- [ ] README / README.ja / config.md; add a graphs scene to `tape/demo-procs.tape` and re-record\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-30T10:24:12Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":127,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Procs view: CPU / memory history graphs"}
